{"files":[{"content":"#include \"knn.h\"\n#include <string.h>\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    char * labels = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\n    float * distances = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * k);\n\n    int i, j, x;\n\n    for (i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        labels[i] = -1;\n        distances[i] = -1;\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n\n        for (j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\n            float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, g.points[j]);\n            int insert_at = k;\n\n            for (x = 0; x < k; x++) {\n                if (d < distances[x] || distances[x] == -1) {\n                    insert_at = x;\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n\n            if (insert_at < k) {\n                if (insert_at + 1 < k) {\n                    size_t shift_count = (size_t)(k - insert_at - 1);\n                    memmove(distances + insert_at + 1, distances + insert_at,\n                            shift_count * sizeof(distances[0]));\n                    memmove(labels + insert_at + 1, labels + insert_at,\n                            shift_count * sizeof(labels[0]));\n                }\n\n                distances[insert_at] = d;\n                labels[insert_at] = g.label;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    qsort(labels, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = labels[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (labels[i] != labels[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n\n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n","path":"src/knn.c"}],"hypothesis":"The top-k insertion search must preserve first-match order, so a SIMD min-index reduction that scans every slot can lose to a scalar early exit. Replacing the dependent overlapping shifts with memmove may let the target C library use optimized vector moves while preserving exact order.","notes":"One bounded experiment; no performance outcome is known. The controller should evaluate correctness and speed.","sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Restore the scalar early-exit scan for the first eligible top-k slot, preserving the same strict comparison and encounter-order tie behavior.","Replace the descending overlapping shifts of the distance and label arrays with memmove calls, guarded when there is no tail to shift."]}